From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FE Fates port <engine@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:04:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] core: frontend: Fire Emblem Fates: growths in Preparations on
 Y

Round 71 (FULL_SWAP_PLAN.md section 5, owner OK "Yes, start round 71"): in
Preparations the Y button (keyboard: the key for Y, A by default) switches the
growth view on the unit panel, one switch per press, the press kept from the
game until let go. Y is taken only while prep_shown(): the Preparations
sequence is alive (sortie::Sequence::GetInstance, the word at 0x006D9030), its
View Map is not running (map::SequenceHuman::GetInstance, 0x006D7BA4, zero)
and the panel shows a unit. No menu of Preparations reads Y (only
MIMassageName and the debug menus override BasicMenuItem::YCall). Everywhere
else Y reaches the game unchanged; Select / Tab / a touch on Growths work as in
round 62.

Preparations' panel (Pick Units, the unit list, Inventory) is the map's panel
without the grid button: the same stat block, so the same boxes. A second
frame check (shows_prep_frame, measured on 2080 robot pictures; no match among
7095 others, none matches both) lets paint() draw there, and only while the
view is on, so with Y never pressed every picture is the round-62 one. Nothing
writes guest memory.

"Settings for this game" (Fire Emblem Fates and mods on its title id) gets one
help line naming the keys: growth_help().

Tests: y_switches_growths_only_in_preparations,
y_reaches_the_game_everywhere_else, select_on_the_map_is_unchanged,
preparations_panel_is_painted_only_while_the_view_is_on,
the_growth_help_names_the_keys_y_is_on.
