+//!
+//! Preparations (round 71, FULL_SWAP_PLAN.md section 5): there **Y** switches the view too, and Y
+//! is kept from the game only while `prep_shown` (no menu of Preparations reads Y: only
+//! `MIMassageName` and the debug menus override `BasicMenuItem::YCall`). On the battle map Y
+//! reaches the game as before and Select stays the key. Preparations' unit panel (Pick Units, the
+//! unit list, Inventory) is the map's panel without the grid button: the same stat block, so the
+//! same boxes; it is painted only while the view is on, so with Y never pressed every picture is
+//! the round-62 one.
+//! - `sortie::Sequence::GetInstance` 0x004BCFD8 returns the word at 0x006D902C + 4, set by the
+//!   Preparations sequence's constructor 0x004BD1CC and cleared by its destructor 0x004BD2F4.
+//! - `map::SequenceHuman::GetInstance` 0x00350D74 returns the word at 0x006D7B90 + 0x14, set by
+//!   `Create` 0x00354604 and cleared by the destructor 0x003545A0. Preparations starts it for
+//!   View Map (its proc list in `__sti___18_SortieSequence_cpp`: SetInfoMap, SequenceHuman::Create,
+//!   SetInfoSortie), where the map cursor has its own keys.
 
 use crate::fates_rando::Guest;
